@{
    ViewBag.Title = "About Durban Harbour";
}

<style>
    body {
        background-color: var(--hc-bg) !important;
        background-image: none !important;
    }

    body::before,
    body::after,
    .hc-home-wrapper::before,
    .hc-home-wrapper::after {
        display: none !important;
    }

    .hc-about-hero {
        background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0d2c54 0%, #1565c0 60%, #00897b 100%);
        color: #ffffff;
        padding: 60px 20px 45px;
        text-align: center;
    }

    .hc-about-hero h1 {
        font-size: 2.6rem;
        font-weight: 800;
        text-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);
        margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    }

    .hc-about-hero p {
        font-size: 1.1rem;
        opacity: 0.92;
        max-width: 580px;
        margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .hc-about-body {
        background: var(--hc-surface);
        color: var(--hc-text);
        border: 1px solid var(--hc-border);
        border-radius: var(--hc-radius);
        box-shadow: var(--hc-shadow);
        padding: 2.2rem 2.5rem;
    }

    .hc-about-body h3 {
        color: var(--hc-heading);
        font-weight: 700;
        margin-top: 1.8rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
        border-left: 4px solid var(--hc-primary);
        padding-left: 0.75rem;
        font-size: 1.15rem;
    }

    .hc-about-body p,
    .hc-about-body li {
        color: var(--hc-text);
        font-size: 0.97rem;
        line-height: 1.85;
    }

    .hc-about-body ul {
        padding-left: 1.3rem;
    }

    .hc-about-body ul li {
        margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
    }

    .hc-fact-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(160px, 1fr));
        gap: 1rem;
        margin-top: 1.2rem;
    }

    .hc-fact-box {
        background: var(--hc-primary-soft);
        border: 1px solid var(--hc-primary-border);
        border-radius: 12px;
        padding: 1.1rem 0.8rem;
        text-align: center;
    }

    .hc-fact-box .hc-fact-num {
        font-size: 1.8rem;
        font-weight: 800;
        color: var(--hc-primary);
        line-height: 1;
    }

    .hc-fact-box .hc-fact-lbl {
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        color: var(--hc-text-muted);
        margin-top: 5px;
    }

    /* Location pin badge */
    .hc-location-badge {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 8px;
        background: var(--hc-primary);
        color: var(--hc-on-primary);
        border-radius: 30px;
        padding: 8px 18px;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    .hc-location-badge span.pin {
        font-size: 1.3rem;
        line-height: 1;
    }

    /* Map container with a pin label on top */
    .hc-map-wrapper {
        position: relative;
        border-radius: 12px;
        overflow: hidden;
        border: 1px solid var(--hc-border);
        box-shadow: var(--hc-shadow);
    }

    .hc-map-label {
        position: absolute;
        top: 14px;
        left: 14px;
        z-index: 10;
        background: #0d2c54;
        color: white;
        padding: 7px 14px;
        border-radius: 20px;
        font-size: 0.82rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 6px;
        box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);
    }
</style>

<div class="hc-about-hero">
    <h1>&#9875; Durban Harbour</h1>
    <p>The biggest and busiest port in Africa, right here in KwaZulu-Natal.</p>
</div>

<div class="container py-5">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-lg-9">
            <div class="hc-about-body">

                <h3>&#127758; What is Durban Harbour?</h3>
                <p>
                    Durban Harbour is a large port on the east coast of South Africa, in the city of Durban,
                    KwaZulu-Natal. It sits along the warm Indian Ocean and is managed by the Transnet National
                    Ports Authority (TNPA). It is the number one busiest port in all of Africa, and one of the
                    top ports in the world.
                </p>

                <div class="hc-fact-grid">
                    <div class="hc-fact-box">
                        <div class="hc-fact-num">&#35;1</div>
                        <div class="hc-fact-lbl">Busiest port in Africa</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="hc-fact-box">
                        <div class="hc-fact-num">57km&sup2;</div>
                        <div class="hc-fact-lbl">Total size of the port</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="hc-fact-box">
                        <div class="hc-fact-num">2.9M+</div>
                        <div class="hc-fact-lbl">Containers handled per year</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="hc-fact-box">
                        <div class="hc-fact-num">1824</div>
                        <div class="hc-fact-lbl">Year it was first built</div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <h3>&#128674; Boat Trips &amp; Leisure</h3>
                <p>
                    The harbour is not just for big ships. People come here to enjoy boat trips on the water.
                    You can go on a harbour cruise, a fishing trip, or a sunset ride across the Indian Ocean.
                    The Point Waterfront area is where most leisure boats depart from - it is a lively and
                    beautiful part of the harbour that is open to the public.
                </p>

                <h3>&#127960;&#65039; Places Inside the Harbour</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Point Waterfront</strong> - where you board boats for leisure trips</li>
                    <li><strong>Wilson's Wharf</strong> - a marina with restaurants and entertainment</li>
                    <li><strong>Durban Yacht Club</strong> - one of the oldest yacht clubs in South Africa</li>
                    <li><strong>Container Terminal</strong> - where big cargo ships load and unload goods</li>
                    <li><strong>The Bluff</strong> - the land on the south side that protects the harbour from big waves</li>
                </ul>

                <h3>&#128031; Sea Life</h3>
                <p>
                    The Indian Ocean around Durban is full of life. You can spot dolphins, different kinds of
                    fish, and even whales during certain times of the year. TNPA works hard to keep the ocean
                    clean and to protect the animals that live in it.
                </p>

                <h3>&#128200; Why It Matters</h3>
                <p>
                    Durban Harbour helps South Africa trade with more than 30 countries around the world.
                    It brings in cars, fuel, and food, and sends out goods like fruit, coal, and steel.
                    The harbour supports hundreds of thousands of jobs for people in KwaZulu-Natal.
                </p>

                <h3>&#128205; Where Is It?</h3>
                <p>The harbour is located at <strong>Point Waterfront, Durban, 4001, KwaZulu-Natal, South Africa.</strong></p>

                <div class="hc-location-badge">
                    <span class="pin">&#128205;</span>
                    Durban Harbour - Point Waterfront, Durban, KZN
                </div>

                <div class="hc-map-wrapper">
                    <div class="hc-map-label">
                        <span>&#128205;</span> Durban Harbour, South Africa
                    </div>
                    <div class="ratio ratio-16x9">
                        <iframe
                            src="https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3462.398!2d31.02541!3d-29.86768!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x1ef7a91247840ff5%3A0xe3c8a41e62800455!2sDurban%20Harbour!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sza!4v1690000000000!5m2!1sen!2sza"
                            style="border:0;"
                            allowfullscreen=""
                            loading="lazy"
                            referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade"
                            title="Durban Harbour location on Google Maps">
                        </iframe>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="mt-4">
                    @Html.ActionLink("Back to Home", "Index", "Home", null, new { @class = "btn btn-primary" })
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
